roduct 1 about 17 above. The 28 order days cost about 1,036 in fees. I rate this the best balance.\n- **0:** Orders every other day, which saves about 518 in fees. Holding two days of stock costs about 460 more in storage, so the net gain is only about +60. It over-orders product 0 by about 41 units (losing about 150–250) and has no buffer for product 1. Expected result is about 150–250 below candidate 3.\n- **4:** Same daily pattern, but with more product 0 than needed and less product 1 buffer. Below candidate 3.\n- **7:** Orders exactly the forecast, about 0.95 × for product 1. Product 1 runs short by roughly 80–90 units, which outweighs the storage it saves on product 0.\n- **2:** Over-orders product 0 even more than candidate 0 and under-orders product 1. Worse than candidate 0.\n- **5:** Orders about 1.2 × forecast for product 0, so it piles up large leftovers and storage costs, and it under-orders product 1.\n- **6:** Orders every third day. It saves about 666 in fees, but carrying about a day of extra stock costs about 940 in storage. It also keeps the same product 0 over-ordering.\n\n**Why the confidence is only 0.4:** Candidates 0, 3 and 4 differ by roughly 100–250 in expected profit. Random swings in demand over 30 days could easily make one of the others come out ahead."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3832, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3832}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T07:52:24.003Z", "request_id": "req_011CgBEFKL6xnzWotDJSi1Th"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event"